Dragonmarks are hereditary arcane sigils that manifest on the skin of individuals from specific bloodlines. They grant spell-like abilities and are the basis of the dragonmarked house system — the powerful economic guilds that dominate commerce across [[Khorvaire]].

!! The Thirteen Marks
|Mark|House|Ability Domain|
|Detection|[[House Medani]]|Divination, threat-sensing|
|Finding|[[House Tharashk]]|Locating people and objects|
|Handling|[[House Vadalis]]|Animal handling and breeding|
|Healing|[[House Jorasco]]|Curative magic|
|Hospitality|[[House Ghallanda]]|Food, shelter, comfort|
|Making|[[House Cannith]]|Artifice and construction|
|Passage|[[House Orien]]|Teleportation and transport|
|Scribing|[[House Sivis]]|Communication and documentation|
|Sentinel|[[House Deneith]]|Protection and mercenary work|
|Shadow|[[House Phiarlan]] / [[House Thuranni]]|Entertainment and espionage|
|Storm|[[House Lyrandar]]|Wind, weather, elemental binding|
|Warding|[[House Kundarak]]|Banking and magical warding|

!! Aberrant Dragonmarks
Marks that appear outside the recognized bloodlines, or that combine traits of multiple marks, are called aberrant. They are unpredictable, sometimes grotesque, and historically persecuted by the twelve houses. [[Mordain the Fleshweaver]] is suspected to bear one.

!! Mark Levels
Marks manifest at three levels of power: Least, Lesser, and Greater. A rare few develop the Siberys Mark, an enormously powerful full-body manifestation.

